    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (84.88) and **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) spearheading the lineup, both benefiting from highly favorable matchups against back-end rotation starters. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** exploits a prime platoon edge against Lodolo, while **Gunnar Henderson** faces the highest xERA of the day (6.56), maximizing his ceiling through sheer volume of high-leverage scoring opportunities. **Kyle Tucker** (80.20) remains an essential start; while his raw park factor is slightly negative, the wind blowing out significantly elevates his power floor, and he remains our primary engine for balancing the 5x5 categories.\n\nThe primary optimization challenge today involved **Luis Lara** (49.98), who sat on the cusp of relevance but ultimately succumbed to a benching due to his lower tier of projected efficiency compared to the high-upside profiles of **Heliot Ramos** (63.09) and **Andy Pages** (64.41). While **Andy Pages** suffers a minor penalty for hitting in the 8-hole, his matchup against the soft-tossing Marte and the favorable wind conditions provide a superior R/RBI profile than what **Luis Lara** could offer. **Josh Jung** (48.39) also narrowly missed the cut; despite a decent spot in the order, his struggle against the quality of Ryan (3.48 xERA) suppressed his score below our threshold for active roster consideration.\n\nInvestors should monitor the efficiency of **Drake Baldwin** (58.03) and **Henry Bolte** (53.78) closely. **Drake Baldwin** carries a lighter score, but his presence in the leadoff spot provides a volume safety net. Conversely, **Henry Bolte** benefits from a strong park factor, though he must navigate a tough assignment against the relatively stingy Brown, whose 3.78 xERA is the most daunting hurdle in today\u2019s starting nine. As always, the priority remains protecting our game caps; however, with the current projected matchups, the configuration of **Coby Mayo**, **Sam Antonacci**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** provides the necessary speed and contact baseline to protect our lead in the scarce stolen base category.",
